@@ -291,6 +291,12 @@ details are similar for other statements/expressions. The method ``emit_write_by
 is a wrapper around the main function ``emit_get_cur_to_write_bytecode()`` that all
 functions must call to emit bytecode.
 
+Stack sizing also accounts for values kept on the stack while control flow is
+unwound. In a ``finally`` block, a pending return or jump keeps its return value
+or jump destination below the unwind sentinel. The compiler reserves an extra
+slot for this value throughout the block, including any nested exception
+handlers, in addition to the slot used by the sentinel or exception.
+
 .. _emitting_native_code:
 
 Emitting native code
